# npm runs every `npm run …` script through this shell. deploy.sh (and the
# `./deploy.sh` call in the "deploy" script) needs bash, and on Windows npm
# would otherwise use cmd.exe. This is Git for Windows' default install path.
#
# On a Linux/macOS machine or a CI host (Netlify, Vercel, GitHub Actions …)
# this path doesn't exist and EVERY npm script fails to start. Override it
# there with the environment variable NPM_CONFIG_SCRIPT_SHELL=/bin/bash
# (environment variables beat .npmrc), or delete this line in that project.
script-shell=C:\\Program Files\\Git\\bin\\bash.exe
